<title>USA: Emons skips preferred dividend.</title>
<headline>Emons skips preferred dividend.</headline>
<dateline>YORK, Pa. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emons Transportation Group Inc said Thursday its board of directors decided to skip the July 1 semi-annual dividend of $0.07 per share on its $0.14 series A cumulative convertible preferred stock.</p>
<p>Including this last omission, the company said it now owes $1.6 million, or $0.98 per share, in past dividends.</p>
<p>The dividend is cumulative and would have to be paid before any dividends on common stock could be paid in the future, Emons added. The company's stock traded at 2-1/2 in the late afternoon, up 1/8.</p>
</text>
